# GraveYield console — environment configuration example.
# Copy to .env.local (dev) or set in your deployment platform.

# ── Snapshot artifact source (P4.1 Step 1) ─────────────────────────────
# The Graveyard reads the grave-indexer ConsoleSnapshotV1 artifact through
# /api/gy/snapshot. Configure EXACTLY ONE source; with neither set, the view
# honestly renders "unavailable" (fail-closed) instead of pretending.
#
#   GY_SNAPSHOT_URL  — HTTPS artifact store (recommended for serverless
#                      deploys such as Vercel, which have no persistent
#                      local directory): publish the indexer's
#                      console-snapshot.json to a release asset / object
#                      storage / any GET endpoint and put its URL here.
#                      Pre-signed URLs work; their query strings are
#                      fetched but never logged or echoed.
#   GY_SNAPSHOT_PATH — absolute path to console-snapshot.json on a mounted
#                      indexer output volume (self-hosted / Docker).
#
# Setting both is rejected (SOURCE_CONFLICT) — the console refuses to guess.
#GY_SNAPSHOT_URL="https://artifacts.example/gy/console-snapshot.json"
#GY_SNAPSHOT_PATH="/var/lib/grave-indexer/console-snapshot.json"

# ── Fleet state source (P4.3 fleet ingestion) ─────────────────────────
# The Salvor Fleet view reads the salvor fleet's JSONL trails
# (monitor-events.jsonl + alerts.jsonl) through /api/gy/fleet. Point this
# at the fleet-ops FLEET_STATE_DIR the operator mounts (self-hosted /
# Docker). Unset → the view honestly renders "unavailable"; it never
# falls back to simulated bots.
#
#   GY_FLEET_STATE_PATH — absolute path to the mounted FLEET_STATE_DIR
#                         (the directory holding the fleet's JSONL trails).
#
# There is deliberately no URL topology here: no upstream publisher of
# fleet trails exists today (see docs/fleet-ingestion.md).
#GY_FLEET_STATE_PATH="/var/lib/salvor-bots/fleet-state"

# Optional freshness budget for the fleet trail in ms (default 1800000 =
# 30 min — 30× the monitor sweep and 6× the scout cycle cadence). Must be
# a positive integer; anything else is rejected, not guessed.
#GY_FLEET_MAX_AGE_MS="1800000"

# ── Wallet connection ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RPC endpoint for the devnet protocol pulse + wallet balance reads.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL="https://api.devnet.solana.com"
